<title>USA: N.Y. business loans off $113 mln in June 18 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans off $113 mln in June 18 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $113 million to $46,248 million in the week ended June 18, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $107 million to $46,514 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $14.633 billion to $874,428 million.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
